# Webstrike Elite's "When you cycle this card, destroy up to one target artifact or enchantment with mana value X" keeps the X
# of the cycling cost paid when it is copied and its targets are chosen anew (CR 707.10, 115.7, 702.29c). Turn 3: Bot1 cycles
# it for X=1 (three Mox Emeralds pay {1}{G}{G}), aiming the trigger at Bot2's first Sol Ring, and copies the trigger with
# Kirol, Attentive First-Year (tapping its two Ornithopters): for the copy, Bot2's Mox Pearl (mana value 0) is refused and the
# second Sol Ring (mana value 1) is chosen. Both Sol Rings are destroyed; the Mox Pearl stays.

